<v Nancy Updike>And that really can be all you need to change your life when you're a teenager-- just one person who thinks you're great. Because chances are, your own sense of yourself is way off. A friend of a friend-- this is a woman in her 50s-- came across an old photo of herself as a teenager.
<v Nancy Updike>当你是青少年时，那真的就是改变你人生所需要的一切——只要有一个人觉得你很棒。因为很有可能，你对自己本身的评价完全错了。一个朋友的朋友——一位50多岁的女性——偶然看到了她十几岁时的一张老照片。

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:53.600
<v Nancy Updike>And it had been years since she'd seen any pictures of herself at that age. And she looked at them and thought, oh, wait, I was pretty. I was pretty. It kind of floored her. Because of course, the girl in the pictures looked nothing like the way she thought of herself at the time. She said she wished she'd known it back then. It would have made a difference.
<v Nancy Updike>她已经很多年没见过自己那个年纪的照片了。她看着它们想，噢，等等，我当时挺漂亮的。这让她感到惊呆了。因为当然，照片里的女孩和她当时的自我认知完全不一样。她说她真希望那时就知道。那会带来很大的改变。

00:36:53.600 --> 00:37:16.160
<v Nancy Updike>Lots of us have had that experience-- looking at old family pictures or yearbooks, seeing things we never saw at the time. This next story is a very specialized case of that kind of thing. It's about the actress Molly Ringwald, who, of course, doesn't just have photos, but movies, beautifully shot, widescreen, full-length Hollywood films of herself as a teenager.
<v Nancy Updike>我们很多人都有过这种经历——看着老家庭照片或年鉴，看到当时从未意识到的东西。下一个故事是一个非常特别的案例。关于女演员Molly Ringwald，当然，她不仅仅有照片，还有电影，宽屏、长篇的好莱坞电影，记录了她十几岁时的样子。

00:37:16.160 --> 00:37:34.770
<v Nancy Updike>She's the redhead, the star, in those three iconic '80s movies by John Hughes-- Pretty in Pink, Sixteen Candles, and The Breakfast Club. Recently, she revisited one of those movies, not exactly by choice, and she talked to Ira Glass. Here's Ira.
<v Nancy Updike>她就是John Hughes执导的那三部80年代经典电影——《粉红佳人》、《十六支蜡烛》和《早餐俱乐部》里的那个红发明星。最近，她重看了其中一部，并不是心甘情愿，她和Ira Glass聊了聊。下面是Ira。

00:37:34.770 --> 00:37:44.760
<v Ira Glass>I suppose it's not a big surprise that Molly Ringwald does not sit around watching old Molly Ringwald films. You know, she's seen 'em. She needs a big reason to go back to them.
