00:37:44.760 --> 00:37:57.300
<v Ira Glass>And recently, her daughter gave her a reason. Her daughter, Mathilda, is 10. And Mathilda wanted to see The Breakfast Club. Of course, 10 is a little young to see The Breakfast Club, but most of her friends had seen it.
<v Ira Glass>最近，她女儿给了她一个理由。她的女儿Mathilda，10岁。Mathilda想看《早餐俱乐部》。当然，10岁看《早餐俱乐部》有点小，但她的朋友大多都看过。

00:37:57.300 --> 00:38:18.870
<v Molly Ringwald>So it was kind of weird that she was the only one that hadn't seen this movie. And she said that it was a conversation at slumber parties where that's a movie that some kids want to watch, and that she had always said, plea-- I don't want to watch it. Can we watch something else? Because she wanted to watch it with me, which I thought was really nice.
<v Molly Ringwald>所以她是唯一没看过这部电影的人，这有点奇怪。她说在睡衣派对上，这是有些孩子想看的电影，而她总是说，拜托……我不想看。我们能看别的吗？因为她想跟我一起看，我觉得这真的很贴心。

00:38:18.870 --> 00:38:39.490
<v Ira Glass>I wonder if it's like she wants to watch it with you-- like, that's a nice thing to say to your mom. But the truth could also be, she just doesn't want to watch it with them. You know what I mean? Like, can you imagine watching your mom with a group of your friends, like, and you have no idea what's about to happen?
<v Ira Glass>我不知道这是不是因为她想跟你一起看——那是一个女儿对妈妈说的好听的话。但真相也可能是，她只是不想跟她们一起看。你懂我的意思吗？比如，你能想象和一群朋友一起看你妈吗，然后你根本不知道会发生什么？

00:38:39.490 --> 00:38:47.410
<v Molly Ringwald>Yeah. I didn't even really think about that, but yeah, I'm sure that had something to do with it. Mathilda does not like surprises.
